    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-10-01T21:18:10+09:30" end-time-local="2026-10-01T21:18:10+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-01T11:48:10Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-01T11:48:10Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A series of troughs continue moving east, with a low pressure system developing near the Victorian border on Friday. In the west, a high pressure system will move into the Bight and slowly move east to be centred over Victoria on Monday, while extending a ridge into parts of the state. Another trough near the WA border is expected to develop from Saturday and extend into the state before weakening by Monday.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW013" description="North West Pastoral" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-10-01T21:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-10-02T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-01T11:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-01T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Slight chance of a shower north of Marla, near zero chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm, possibly severe with damaging winds, large hail and heavy rain which may lead to flash flooding north of Marla. Winds south to southwesterly 15 to 25 km/h.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-10-02T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-10-03T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-01T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-02T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Medium chance of showers north of Marla, most likely in the morning. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm north of Coober Pedy. Winds southeast to southwesterly 20 to 30 km/h. Overnight temperatures falling to between 8 and 14 with daytime temperatures reaching the low to mid 20s.</text>
                <text type="fire_danger">Moderate</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 8:40am to 3:50pm, UV Index predicted to reach 10 [Very High]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-10-03T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-10-04T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-02T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-03T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. The chance of fog south of Woomera in the early morning. Medium chance of showers north of Coober Pedy, most likely from the late morning. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm west of Coober Pedy. Winds south to southeasterly 15 to 20 km/h tending northeast to southeasterly 15 to 25 km/h in the early morning. Overnight temperatures falling to between 7 and 13 with daytime temperatures reaching 20 to 25.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-10-04T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-10-05T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-03T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-04T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. High chance of showers west of Coober Pedy, medium chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm north of Coober Pedy in the morning and afternoon. Winds northeast to southeasterly 15 to 25 km/h becoming light during the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 9 and 14 with daytime temperatures reaching the low to mid 20s.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="4" start-time-local="2026-10-05T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-06T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-04T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-05T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. The chance of morning fog west of Coober Pedy. Slight chance of a shower north of Coober Pedy, near zero chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm north of Coober Pedy in the afternoon and evening. Light winds becoming west to southwesterly 15 to 20 km/h during the afternoon then tending south to southwesterly during the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 11 and 14 with daytime temperatures reaching the mid to high 20s.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
